Description: Kidux sign-in and lock screens
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This package is
 the screen the machine boots into, where each child taps their own picture
 and types their own password, and the screen that locks a running session
 when the time is up or the power button is pressed.
 .
 Both run as the greeter's system user, out of reach of anything a child can
 run, and they are the only places an adult ever types the adult password.
